<title>FRANCE: Kok says did not discuss any EMU delay with Chirac.</title>
<headline>Kok says did not discuss any EMU delay with Chirac.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Prime Minister Wim Kok said after talks with French President Jacques Chirac on Wednesday that they had not discussed any delay in European Economic and Monetary Union.</p>
<p>&quot;We know that in the first half of next year decisions are going to be taken on the basis of the criteria and the timetable so there is no need to have further discussion at this moment on that,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
<p>Asked if there had been any discussion of delay, he said &quot;No&quot;.</p>
<p>European Union leaders are due to decide in early 1998 which countries qualify for a single currency when it is first launched in January 1999.</p>
</text>
